WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.301
Want to bring in Misty Marris.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.702
She was a trial attorney.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.404
And Areva Martin, an attorney

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.573
and legal affairs commentator. Areva.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.841
This was really a preview

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.110
of what we should expect to be presented

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.611
during this trial.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.914
What was your biggest takeaway?

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.149
Yeah, my biggest takeaway

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:18.351
is that this defense attorney is good

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.886
and he came out of the gate

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.421
and he challenged

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.288
the jury

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.990
to basically disregard

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.991
everything they had heard

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:25.925
from the prosecutor.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.360
He said, look, these are not facts.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.495
These are theories.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.396
And then he did something

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.097
that I thought was really good.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.298
He had Mr.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.834
Murdaugh stand up and he personalized it.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.069
He said, look at this guy.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.204
This is not the guy that would butcher

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.339
and brutalize

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:39.939
his son,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.641
that he was just riding around

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.476
in a car bonding.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.411
He wouldn't, you know,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.712
shoot his son in the head.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.447
So his brains literally

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.516
would explode out of his head.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.684
And he talked about the amount of blood

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.420
that would be on anyone that,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.721
you know, someone in that fashion.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.623
Then he talked about the timeline,

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.591
that the timeline doesn't work,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.793
that there wasn't enough time

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.760
for someone to commit

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.895
these brutal murders,

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.896
go back to their home,

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:03.930
clean up their body,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.831
change their clothes,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.932
and then get in the car

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.367
and exit that property.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.135
So he gave the jurors

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.470
lots of things

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.106
that they could use to create doubt.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.240
And he basically said,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.710
look here right now, he is innocent.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.079
He did not do this.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.113
And so I think that was

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.714
a very powerful statement

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.383
by the defense jury.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:23.817
Yeah.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.818
I mean, he did everything

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.219
he could in those opening arguments

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.721
to try to humanize his client. Right.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.390
Having them stand up, talking about what

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.125
a loving and doting father he was

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.960
and that there was a Snapchat video

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.295
not long before with his son

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.896
where they were laughing.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.731
And then you had the prosecutor

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.532
come out of the gate

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.701
and talk about this video

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.203
that he said was taken

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.705
just before the murders at that kennel.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:46.172
And he says,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.442
you can hear Alex's voice in that video,

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.510
which undercuts

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.711
what he told police,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.579
that he was in the home

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.547
napping after dinner and wasn't there.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.516
How dare mean is that

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.084
for the defendant, Misty

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.020
So right now, what

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.821
we expect to see

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.124
a trial is a lot of inconsistencies,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.525
according to the prosecutor,

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.094
with respect to those videos.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.863
The body cam footage

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.931
that shows what Alec Paul said

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.567
as opposed to what the timeline

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.903
the prosecution is going to put together,

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.472
all seemingly from cell phone data.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.340
This video

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.541
that puts him in a place

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.443
he said he was not at the time.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.844
So that's certainly going to be

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.012
something that will play out.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.414
But we saw the defense get ahead of this.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.183
And to read this, to

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:30.817
sort of flip

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.218
the script and say,

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.088
well, the prosecution's own experts

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.956
are going to put together a timeline

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.491
that simply isn't feasible.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.726
Another bombshell

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.127
coming out of the defense

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.362
opening statement,

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.230
this foreshadowing

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.399
of an alternate theory of the case.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.066
It seems like

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.401
this could have been only done

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.802
by two people.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:50.503
That's something

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.804
I think we're going to see more of

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.772
as this case goes on.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.840
Alternate theories

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.575
proposed by the defense.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:55.909
All right.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.010
I want to bring in Diane Gallagher

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:57.877
She is there right

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.778
outside the courthouse.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.613
She's been following this, Diane.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.915
It's that, as we were just talking about,

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:02.782
the cell phone data

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.117
and the defense attorney

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.084
was trying to cast

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.553
doubt about the data,

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.454
saying that there were inconsistencies.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.289
And he had said

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:09.856
Maggie's

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.992
phone was used up until 8:54 p.m..

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.028
We heard the state prosecutor, I know

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.763
did say that her phone stopped

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:19.899
and locked, I believe, at 8:49 p.m.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.334
the same time, around the same time

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:21.834
as Paul.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.969
So already

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.270
you see the defense attorney

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.106
there trying to raise doubts, poke holes

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.442
in the state prosecution's argument

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.146
Precisely, Pamela.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.582
And look, you also noticed

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.016
that the defense attorney,

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.251
Dick Harpootlian,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:41.521
said that they that he asked who

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.056
who unlocked that phone

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.190
for law enforcement,

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.025
saying that it was Alex Murdaugh

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.328
who unlocked Maggie Murdaugh's phone

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:49.862
for them to go through.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.463
Now, look,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.765
the state went through a bit

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.900
at the beginning

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.335
explaining what the words

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.937
circumstantial evidence means and telling

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.340
people what reasonable doubt

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.609
means, trying to go over the definitions

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:03.910
of those specifically.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.777
That has been something

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.946
that the defense has said all along.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.181
But specifically this week

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.350
when going over those pretrial motions

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.718
about the evidence

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.852
and the experts

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.020
that the prosecution

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.356
wants to introduce into this trial,

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.057
talking about the fact

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.493
that much of this is circumstantial

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.762
there's no smoking gun per se.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.797
They don't have the weapon.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:25.765
They acknowledge

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:26.833
they do not have the weapon,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.968
although the judge did tell them

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.970
they could use a ballistics expert.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.538
This was a pretrial motion

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.673
who says that

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:34.407
the casings

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.975
that were found in those

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.443
around the crime scene

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.745
and on the hunting property

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.179
in a firing range area

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.548
do match that missing weapon

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:43.716
that is sort of

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.852
at the center of all of this.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:46.819
Now, again,

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.854
there is some discrepancy

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.222
between what the defense claims

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.590
and what they claim as well.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.258
Something we're going to see continue

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.693
on, of course, in the coming days

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.994
is could go up to three weeks,

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.162
we're told.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:56.496
Yeah.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.163
And it's interesting

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.399
how both sides try to spin

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.334
whatever the evidence is in their favor.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.602
Right. That 911 call.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.470
Prosecutors say, listen to this.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.972
You know, really listen closely.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:06.673
The defense attorney

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:09.342
said, I want you to listen to that.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.611
Also emphasizing,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.346
you know, the role that he played

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.281
in opening the phone for police

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.949
and that he called

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.218
he called Maggie's phone several times.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.687
After she was killed.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:21.954
And you know that

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.022
the prosecutor is saying

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.257
he was trying to create an alibi.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.291
The defense saying, look,

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.693
that shows you right there

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.027
he didn't know what was going on.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.629
He wasn't involved in this so,

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:30.763
so many different threads

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.498
and pieces of evidence to follow in this.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.566
This is just the beginning.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.301
Diane Gallagher, Misty Marris, Areva

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:36.336
Martin, thank you all.

